        "cnm_096"
      ],
      "explanation": "The positive coefficients let us rule out positive roots without solving the cubic. For every \\(x\\geq 0\\), the variable terms are nonnegative, so\n\\[\nx^3+6x^2+11x+6\\geq 6>0.\n\\]\nThus no nonnegative number can satisfy the equation. There is a negative real root, since substituting \\(x=-1\\) gives\n\\[\n-1+6-11+6=0.\n\\]\nThis also rules out the choices claiming no negative roots or no real roots. The equation has no positive real roots, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
